        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ലിഫ്റ്റ്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ലിഫ്റ്റ് — liphṟṟŭ — \"a lift\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ലിഫ്റ്റ് കേടായതുകൊണ്ട് ഞങ്ങൾ നടന്നു കയറി. liphṟṟŭ kēṭāyatukoṇṭŭ ñaṅṅaḷ naṭannu kayaṟi. Because the lift had broken down, we walked up."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "British usage: Malayalam says ലിഫ്റ്റ് (liphṟṟŭ), not elevator."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ലിഫ്റ്റ് (liphṟṟŭ) was borrowed from English lift, a moving box that carries people between floors."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
